Third-party components
----------------------

None. Memory Palace has no third-party dependency and no CDN.

Vendored from this project's own kits (same licence, same author), copied verbatim on 26/11/2026:

- web-kit 0.1.0 — docs/play/web-kit.js — the offline shell, storage helpers and PWA registration
- export-kit 1.0.0 — docs/play/export-kit.js — Blob download, used for the palace export

Neither kit is modified. Neither makes a network request.

Not a flashcard app
-------------------

There is no interval, ease factor, due date or repetition schedule in this app, and no score, grade or
streak. The palace is the method: you place things in a room and walk the room back. A test reports what you
got right and wrong in order, and shows each miss at the spot it belonged to — it does not rate you.

The ten-per-room cap
--------------------

A room holds ten. An eleventh is REFUSED and the refusal names the item it would have displaced, because a
memory palace that silently drops a thing is worse than one that says the room is full.
